{%- comment -%}
  MY TAPE STORE — ABANDONED CART  ·  Shopify Email "Custom Liquid" block

  NOT THE SAME EMAIL AS 06
  06 is abandoned CHECKOUT: they reached payment and stopped. Warm, close to
  done, so that one pushes — "Complete my order".
  This is abandoned CART: they added items and never started checkout. Colder,
  often still comparing or unsure which product suits the job. Pushing a
  half-decided buyer to "buy now" is what makes these emails feel like spam, so
  this one stays out of the way and lets the cart link do the asking.

  WHERE THIS GOES
  Marketing > Automations > Abandoned cart > edit the email, then:
    1. header/logo block image -> mts-email-header-white.png, width maximum
    2. delete every OTHER block
    3. keep ONE Custom Liquid block and paste all of this into it
  The footer with the unsubscribe link stays — it is legally required.

  VARIABLES — CHECK THE PREVIEW
  Shopify Email's abandoned-cart scope differs from abandoned-checkout. The
  loop and the link are both written with fallbacks. If the preview comes back
  empty, try the bare names without a prefix. The cart link must work; the rest
  is decoration if it does not.

  Same construction as 06: fluid tables so it reflows to 320px with no media
  query, explicit backgrounds on every cell, 128px images in a 64px box with
  real alt text, and an 18px bold button label so white on #df3c22 clears the
  large-text contrast bar.
{%- endcomment -%}

<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
       style="background:#f4f2ef;margin:0;padding:0;width:100%;">
  <tr><td align="center" style="padding:0;background:#f4f2ef;">

    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
           style="width:100%;max-width:600px;background:#ffffff;">

      <!-- headline -->
      <tr><td style="padding:28px 22px 0 22px;background:#ffffff;
          font-family:'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">
        <div style="display:inline-block;background:#fdeae5;color:#b62f18;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;
             letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;padding:6px 11px;border-radius:6px;">
          Saved in your cart
        </div>
        <h1 style="margin:15px 0 0 0;font-size:25px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:700;color:#1f1f1f;
            letter-spacing:-0.4px;">
          Still deciding{% if customer.first_name %}, {{ customer.first_name }}{% endif %}?
        </h1>
        <p style="margin:10px 0 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#555050;">
          No rush — it'll be here when you are.
        </p>
      </td></tr>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <tr><td style="padding:22px 22px 0 22px;background:#ffffff;">
        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr>
          <td align="center" style="background:#df3c22;border-radius:7px;">
            <a href="{{ cart.url | default: checkout.abandoned_checkout_url | default: shop.url }}"
               style="display:block;padding:16px 24px;font-family:'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
                      font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none;text-align:center;">
              View my cart
            </a>
          </td>
        </tr></table>
      </td></tr>

      <!-- items -->
      <tr><td style="padding:28px 22px 0 22px;background:#ffffff;
          font-family:'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">
        <div style="border-top:1px solid #e6e1da;padding-top:18px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;
             letter-spacing:1.3px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a8480;">
          In your cart
        </div>
      </td></tr>

      {%- comment -%} assign first: `default` is a filter and cannot sit inside a for expression {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign cart_lines = cart.line_items | default: checkout.line_items -%}
      {% for line in cart_lines %}
      <tr><td style="padding:14px 22px 0 22px;background:#ffffff;
          font-family:'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">
        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr>
          <td width="64" valign="top" style="width:64px;padding-right:14px;">
            {% if line.image %}
              <img src="{{ line.image | img_url: '128x128' }}"
                   alt="{{ line.title | escape }}" width="64" height="64"
                   style="display:block;width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:8px;
                          border:1px solid #e6e1da;background:#f4f2ef;
                          font-family:'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
                          font-size:10px;color:#8a8480;">
            {% else %}
              <div style="width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:8px;background:#f4f2ef;border:1px solid #e6e1da;">&nbsp;</div>
            {% endif %}
          </td>
          <td valign="middle" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;">
            <div style="font-weight:600;color:#1f1f1f;font-size:15px;">{{ line.title }}</div>
            {% if line.variant.title and line.variant.title != 'Default Title' %}
              <div style="color:#8a8480;font-size:13px;margin-top:2px;">{{ line.variant.title }}</div>
            {% endif %}
            <div style="color:#555050;font-size:13px;margin-top:2px;">Qty {{ line.quantity }}</div>
          </td>
        </tr></table>
      </td></tr>
      {% endfor %}

      <!-- volume pricing -->
      <tr><td style="padding:24px 22px 34px 22px;background:#ffffff;
          font-family:'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">
        <div style="font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#555050;">
          Volume pricing applies automatically —
          <strong style="color:#b62f18;">5%</strong> from 2 units,
          <strong style="color:#b62f18;">10%</strong> from 6,
          <strong style="color:#b62f18;">15%</strong> from 10.
        </div>
      </td></tr>

    </table>
  </td></tr>
</table>
